<title>UK: TENNIS-DAVIS CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-DAVIS CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Davis Cup tennis matches on Sunday:</p>
<p>Euro/African zone group two play-offs</p>
<p>In Jurmala: Latvia beat Ghana 3-1</p>
<p>Frank Ofori (Ghana) beat Girt Dzelde (Latvia) 7-6 (7-5) 6-4.</p>
<p>Note: The second reverse singles game was not played as Latvia had taken an unbeatable 3-0 lead after Saturday's doubles.  </p>
<p>Asia/Oceania zone group one</p>
<p>In Tashkent: Japan beat Uzbekistan 3-2</p>
<p>Oleg Ogorodov (Uzbekistan) beat Goichi Motomura (Japan) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>6-2</p>
<p>Hideki Kaneko (Japan) beat Dmitry Tomashevich (Uzbekistan) 6-3</p>
<p>4-6 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>Euro/African zone group one play-off</p>
<p>In Kiev: Britain beat Ukraine 3-2</p>
<p>Andrei Medvedev (Ukraine) beat Tim Henman (Britain) 6-7 (5-7) 6-3 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Greg Rusedski (Britain) beat Andrei Rybalko (Ukraine) 7-5 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Euro/African zone group two, second round</p>
<p>In Nova Gorica: Norway beat Slovenia 4-1</p>
<p>Jan Frode Andersen (Norway) beat Iztok Bozic (Slovenia) 6-3 1-6 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Christian Ruud (Norway) beat Blaz Trupej (Slovenia) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>In Bytom: Poland beat Ivory Coast 4-1</p>
<p>Bartlomiej Dabrowski (Poland) beat Claude N'Goran (Ivory Coast) 6-4 6-1 6-0</p>
<p>Michal Chmela (Poland) beat Nouhoun Sangare (Ivory Coast) 6-1 6-2</p>
<p>Euro/African zone group two, second round:</p>
<p>In Maia, Portugal: Portugal beat Yugoslavia 3-2</p>
<p>Bojan Vujic (Yugoslavia) beat Joao Cunha e Silva (Portugal) 6-4 6-3 3-6 4-6 6-3</p>
<p>Emanuel Couto (Portugal) beat Nenad Zimonjic (Yugoslavia) 6-7 (2-7) 7-5 7-5 6-3</p>
</text>
